<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Todora — dependency licenses</title>
<style>
body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 70rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
section { border-top: 1px solid #aaa; margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
<h1>Todora — dependency licenses</h1>
<p>Generated with cargo-about 0.9.2 from the workspace's locked dependencies,
including build dependencies and all supported Mac and Linux targets.
Some entries may not be used by a particular binary.</p>
<p>Todora's own license is in <a href="LICENSE">LICENSE</a>.
Separate asset licenses and credits are listed in <a href="LICENSES.md">LICENSES.md</a>.</p>
<p>Dependency source links below open the exact published crate version's source archive.
The Symphonia crates are provided under MPL 2.0; their source is available through
these links. Todora uses the published crates without local modifications.</p>
{{#each licenses}}
<section>
<h2>{{name}}</h2>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
<li>{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}} —
{{#if crate.source}}
<a href="https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}/download">source archive</a>
{{else}}
<a href="https://github.com/oliverlukschander/todora">Todora source</a>
{{/if}}
{{#if crate.repository}} · <a href="{{crate.repository}}">upstream project</a>{{/if}}</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</html>
